     "I have found the problem, but I have not found (yet) a robust solution. \r<br>The problem is related to bivariate tables that contain lots of zeroes, eg\r<br>\r<br> &gt; table(input$y.cdi5.t0,  input$y.cdi8.t0)\r<br>\r<br>       0   1   2\r<br>   0 212  12   9\r<br>   1   2   0   0\r<br>   2   1   0   0\r<br>\r<br>Usually, this is not problematic, but in this case, it clearly is. \r<br>Perhaps because there are several sparse bivariate tables, all involving \r<br>the same variable(s). Removing one of these variables (eg y.cdi5.t0) \r<br>seems to solve the problem.\r<br>\r<br>Yves.\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
